# Frontend Standards

## Stack
- React 19 + TypeScript 5.x + Vite
- react-router-dom for routing
- recharts for charts (no D3 directly)
- No CSS framework — hand-crafted CSS in index.css

## Patterns
- All API calls go through `src/api/client.ts` — never call fetch directly in components
- Use `useFetch<T>` hook for data loading with loading/error states
- TypeScript interfaces in `src/types/index.ts` must match backend Java DTOs
- Pages go in `src/pages/`, shared components in `src/components/`
- Format currency with `formatCurrency()` from Shared.tsx (INR, ₹ symbol)

## Rules
- No `any` type unless wrapping an untyped API response
- No inline styles — use CSS classes from index.css
- All numbers from the backend are monetary — display with formatCurrency()
- Frontend does NO financial calculations — all math happens on the backend
